==========================================================================
 LAS parameter set: n=4 ell=4 kappa=60 gamma=122880  (N=256, Q=8380417)
   M = n + ell = 8   (dim of sk=r, witness r', mask y_mask, responses z_hat/z)
   paper notation: pp=(A,H)  pk=t  sk=r  statement Y=t'  witness r' (=y_witness)
   signing mask y_mask -> commitment w = A*y_mask  (hashed into c; NOT transmitted)
==========================================================================
 Reproducibility: compiler=13.3.0
                  built=Jun 25 2026 17:40:33   git=ad3448c (main)
                  (CPU / OS-WSL / run-date captured per run by
                   scripts/run_fair_benchmarks.sh into metadata.txt)
 10 runs x 1000 iters/op; mean +/- sample SD; single thread, -O3.
 One setup and one consistent state per run; primary protocol timings first,
 then diagnostics from the SAME state (cost-attribution / communication aids).

--- WHAT IS COMPARED (separate base/adaptor modules; matched parameters; shared primitives) ---
 BASE  (simplified Dilithium-style signature; NO adaptor statement t'):
   Sign      c = H(pk, w,      M)        Verify    c == H(pk, w',      M)
 LAS ADAPTOR (same scheme; statement/lock Y=t' folded into the hash):
   PreSign   c = H(pk, w + t', M),  z_hat = y_mask + c*r  (reject |z_hat|inf > gamma-kappa-1)
   PreVerify c == H(pk, w' + t', M)
   Adapt     z = z_hat + r'   (final response z;          reject |z|inf > gamma-kappa)
   Ext / Extract   s = z - z_hat   (recovers the witness r')
   Adapted sig clears ordinary Verify without an explicit +t' because
     A(z_hat + r') - c*t = (A*z_hat - c*t) + A*r' = w' + t'   (t' = A*r').
   pi (paper-level off-chain proof of well-formedness) is NOT implemented/measured here.

##########################################################################
# PRIMARY (protocol-level) timings -- the headline adaptor-overhead table #
##########################################################################
--- COMPUTATION (microseconds, mean +/- sample SD) ---

 Shared (public params pp=(A,H); KeyGen -> pk=t, sk=r):
   Setup             51.57 +/-   6.64
   KeyGen            62.04 +/-   2.69

 Base path (simplified Dilithium-style, c = H(pk, w, M); no t'):
   Sign             632.39 +/-  26.11
   Verify           149.97 +/-   3.26

 LAS adaptor path (statement t' folded into the hash, c = H(pk, w+t', M)):
   PreSign          653.04 +/-  23.23
   PreVerify        156.75 +/-   5.34
   Adapt            161.31 +/-   5.15
   Ext / Extract     54.51 +/-   8.28

 Adaptor overhead (adaptor op vs the base op it mirrors):
   PreSign       vs Sign       653.04 vs   632.39   (+3.3%)
   PreVerify     vs Verify     156.75 vs   149.97   (+4.5%)
   Adapt         vs Verify     161.31 vs   149.97   (+7.6%)
   Ext / Extract (separate)     54.51            (no base analogue)

##########################################################################
# DIAGNOSTICS (secondary; cost-attribution & communication; SAME state)  #
##########################################################################
--- A. REJECTION-SAMPLING DISTRIBUTION (2000 signing calls each;
       attempts read directly from base_attempts / las_attempts) ---
   operation                   avg accept%   min   max   p50   p95
   Base Sign (no t')         2.720   36.8%     1    17     2     7
   LAS PreSign (folds t')    2.756   36.3%     1    15     2     7
   avg = mean attempts/sig; accept% = 1/avg; both schemes reject under
   Fiat-Shamir-with-aborts at the bound gamma-kappa (Base Sign) /
   gamma-kappa-1 (LAS PreSign).

--- B. ADAPT TIMING CLARIFICATION (microseconds, mean +/- SD) ---
   Adapt checked total       161.306 +/-  5.154   (PROTOCOL: las_adapt above, incl. internal PreVerify)
   witness-add only            4.742 +/-  0.197   (DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: z=z_hat+r'; not a protocol op)
   A real Adapt MUST pre-verify first; the witness-add line is a lower bound,
   not a usable operation.  Use 'Adapt checked total' for protocol cost.

--- C. COMMUNICATION (packed bytes; BYTE-LEVEL only, NOT EVM gas) ---
   public key    pk = t                2944
   secret key    sk = r                 512
   statement     Y = t'               2944   (63.0% of the signature; t' has pk size)
   witness       r' = y_witness        512   (same packed layout as sk = r)
   challenge     c                      64
   response      z (final)            4608   (98.6% of the signature)
   response      z_hat (pre-sig)      4608   (same packed layout as z)
   signature         (c, z)           4672
   pre-signature     (c, z_hat)       4672   (same size as the signature)
   final adapted sig (c, z)           4672   (an ordinary signature)
   commitment    w = A*y_mask       internal computed commitment; hashed into c; not transmitted
   -- protocol-component catalogue (context; what each object is / why counted or not) --
   pp=(A,H)  A' seed                    32   (public params; only this 32-byte seed is transmitted)
   pp=(A,H)  expanded A'             11776   (n*ell polys; DERIVED from the seed, NOT transmitted)
   y_mask (signing mask, S_gamma)    4608   (n+ell polys; INTERNAL, hashed into c via w, NOT transmitted)
   w = A*y_mask (commitment)         2944   (n polys; INTERNAL, hashed into c, NOT transmitted)
   pi (NIZK well-formedness proof)    n/a   (paper-level off-chain proof; NOT implemented / NOT measured)
   tx metadata (addrs/amounts/nonces) excl   (application/ledger layer; EXCLUDED from this accounting)
   atomic-swap payload (byte-level only):
     off-chain   = Y + 2*pre-signature        =  12288   [= t' + 2*(c, z_hat)]
     settlement  = 2*signature                =   9344   [= 2*(c, z)]
     settlement incl. escrowed Y = Y + 2*sig  =  12288
   (EVM/keccak gas for on-chain verification is a separate axis; see evm/.)

--- D. COMPONENT MICROBENCHMARKS (microseconds, mean +/- SD) ---
   Cost-attribution ESTIMATES timing LOCAL COPIES of the inner steps
   (behaviourally identical to las.c) -- NOT the protocol entry points above.
   A-product / commitment w = A*y_mask                    47.146 +/-  2.120
   challenge hash  c = H(pk, w(+t'), M)                   50.794 +/-  0.578
   c*r  (one response polynomial; c is sparse)            11.291 +/-  0.525
   c*r  (all LAS_M response polynomials)                  91.962 +/-  7.033
   norm check  |z|inf over n+ell polys                     2.018 +/-  0.077
   w + t'   (n polys)                                      4.902 +/-  0.048
   z_hat + witness r'   (n+ell polys)                      4.742 +/-  0.197
   c*t  (all LAS_N public-key polys; Verify/PreVerify)    44.444 +/-  1.274
   KeyGen/Gen: sample r (n+ell ternary polys)              7.134 +/-  0.115
     (KeyGen = sample r + A*r; A*r is the A-product line above; statement Y gen = KeyGen)
   Ext: s = z - z_hat   (n+ell polys)                      4.648 +/-  0.187
   Ext: A*s   (recompute statement; = an A-product)       46.221 +/-  1.519
   Ext: t' == A*s check   (n polys)                        0.474 +/-  0.034
   note: a full Sign/PreSign attempt applies c*r across LAS_M = n+ell = 8
         response polynomials; Verify-style challenge multiplication applies
         c*t across LAS_N = n = 4 public-key polynomials.

--- E. NORM-MARGIN DIAGNOSTICS (achieved infinity-norm vs the reject bound;
       max over the 2000 sampled accepted signatures from section A) ---
   accepted |z|inf      max    122820   vs accept limit g-k   =    122820   (100.00% of band)
   accepted |z^|inf     max    122819   vs accept limit g-k-1 =    122819   (100.00% of band)
   Interpretation: the RESPONSE z/z^ saturates its band (~100%) -- the bound is
   the binding constraint and is exactly why ~63% of attempts are rejected.
   Contrast the AMHL cumulative WITNESS ||s_j||inf, which is tiny (<=K) vs the
   g-k-K band: that bound is extremely loose (see bench_app, the K-series table).
